# SRG-APP-000316-WSR-000170  -  CAT II
# The web server must provide the capability to immediately disconnect or
# disable remote access to the hosted applications.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000316-WSR-000170
group:           V-206418
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-002322
control_rev5:    AC-17

contribution:    Splunk owns several levers for an immediate disconnect - startwebserver 0
                 or httpport 0 stops the Splunk Web listener, disabled on an input stanza
                 stops a receiver, and a "!" deny rule in acceptFrom blocks a source on any
                 listener - and all of them are available whether or not a site has
                 declared the keys.

external:        The administrator's authority and the organizational procedure for
                 ordering and executing an immediate disconnect sit outside the
                 application.
external:        The check also requires that the disconnect methods be documented so the
                 right action is taken during an attack; that is a document, not a setting.
external:        Network-level isolation of the instance during an attack is carried by the
                 hosting network, and host-level service control by the operating system.

manual_reason:   The requirement is a capability, and the capability is present in the
                 product whichever way the keys are left; no value decides it, so an
                 assessor confirms the methods and their documentation rather than reading
                 a setting.

citation:        Every condition in the reviewed criterion is a present test on a key whose
                 absence is normal and whose presence proves nothing. The check makes a
                 finding only where "the web server is not capable of or cannot be
                 configured to disconnect or disable remote access", and the capability
                 exists in the product regardless: startwebserver defaults to 1 with "0
                 disables Splunk Web" (web.conf.spec:23-26), httpport defaults to 8000 and
                 "If omitted or 0 the server will NOT start an http listener"
                 (web.conf.spec:28-33), and acceptFrom defaults to "*" while accepting a
                 "!" prefix "to cause the rule to reject the connection"
                 (web.conf.spec:1080-1096). Requiring those keys present reports a finding
                 against an instance that is fully capable of the disconnect, which is
                 over-reach of the worst kind because the thing demanded has no bearing on
                 the thing checked; worse, requiring startwebserver or httpport to be
                 declared tells an assessor nothing about whether an administrator can act.
                 The inputs.conf disabled condition carries an empty stanza name and cannot
                 be evaluated at all. The two acceptFrom non_empty conditions duplicate
                 SRG-APP-000315-WSR-000004, where the check text actually asks for a
                 restriction. No value decides this requirement, so it is a manual
                 confirmation.
finding:         Not expected to be a finding against the application: Splunk can stop its
                 web listener, disable an individual input, or reject a source with a deny
                 rule, and an assessor confirms these methods are documented; raise a
                 finding only where the documented procedure does not exist.
